  "title": "Zai Lab Announces Dosing of First Participant in Global Phase 1/1b study of ZL-1503, an IL-13/IL-31R Bispecific Antibody for the Treatment of Atopic Dermatitis",
  "summary": "In preclinical studies, ZL-1503 demonstrated the ability to simultaneously suppress inflammatory and pruritogenic (itch-causing) pathways implicated in AD. These findings, recently presented at the European Academy of Allergy and Clinical Immunology (EAACI) 2025 Congress, highlight ZL-1503’s potential as a novel therapeutic option for patients with moderate-to-severe AD. “The progress of ZL-1503 is another strong example […]",
